WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.451
Exercise 9: define business concepts once and link your contracts to them.

2
00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:15.884
Write the whole ontology in one file. The prefix ecom gives every concept a stable IRI.

3
00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:25.023
Entities Order and Article, their properties, and how they relate.

4
00:00:25.073 --> 00:00:26.974
Load the API key and host into your shell.

5
00:00:27.024 --> 00:00:37.857
Upload the file in one go. One PUT replaces the whole namespace.

6
00:00:37.907 --> 00:00:46.722
All five concepts are there.

7
00:00:46.772 --> 00:01:01.970
Link the contract fields to the concepts: authoritativeDefinitions with the IRI as url.

8
00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:10.198
The contracts stay valid.

9
00:01:10.248 --> 00:01:22.972
Re-publish the linked contracts.

10
00:01:23.022 --> 00:01:27.960
Open Semantics. Your namespace E-Commerce is there.

11
00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:35.063
The two entities, Order and Article. Switch to the diagram.

12
00:01:35.113 --> 00:01:44.386
Open Article, then its property SKU.

13
00:01:44.436 --> 00:01:53.891
SKU: defined once, with its own IRI.

14
00:01:53.941 --> 00:02:01.458
The reverse lookup: every data product that uses an SKU.

15
00:02:01.508 --> 00:02:10.471
On the SKU Sales page, its business concepts appear under Semantics.
